  "introduction": "Build on earlier mathematics by studying divisibility rules and prime factorisation.",
  "definition": "A number is divisible by another when division leaves no remainder. A number is divisible by 2 if its last digit is even, by 3 if its digit sum is divisible by 3, by 5 if its last digit is 0 or 5, by 9 if its digit sum is divisible by 9, and by 10 if it ends in 0. Prime factorisation expresses a positive integer greater than 1 as a product of primes.",
